  "body": "In HTML documents, SVG and MathML title, style, script, and noscript are tokenized as RCDATA, except that comments and processing instructions are still recognized, CDATA sections become text without their markers, and a DOCTYPE is dropped. Their end tag always ends them, also inside a comment, processing instruction, or CDATA section. SVG and MathML textarea, xmp, iframe, noembed, noframes, and plaintext break out of foreign content, also when self-closing. SVG title is no longer an HTML integration point, a special element, or in the default scope, and the content models of SVG title, style, and script in HTML documents are text. Fragment parsing and template for patching are updated so these elements cannot hold their own end tag.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/65512.\nPart of #11397.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * …\n   * …\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/65512\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n- [ ] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: n/a\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n---\n\nThis is step 2 of the plan in [#11397 (comment)](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11397#issuecomment-7017950358). The parse errors for today's parsing are a separate PR (step 1, #13301), and both edit the same text; this PR should undo the step 1 parse errors that become dead when this is closer to ready (step 8). The insertion errors (an element, or a comment or PI containing `</`, inserted into these elements from elsewhere) stay meaningful.\n\nNotes:\n\n- The tokenizer text adds the foreign RCDATA state and a single rule: while the foreign RCDATA flag is true, before each tokenizer step, the element's end tag is recognized and acts like the end of the input in the current state, so comments, bogus comments, processing instructions, and CDATA sections inside the element end at it. Comment, bogus comment, PI, and CDATA states now switch to a return state instead of the data state.\n- Fragment parsing into such an element uses the foreign RCDATA state with the flag false, so comments and PIs aren't recognized there and CDATA markers are still dropped.\n- `template for` patching into these elements keeps text, drops comments and PIs that contain `</`, and doesn't insert element children (they stay detached, including when the adoption agency moves them).\n- Checked with a patched html5lib that follows this text (tree and error counts for the new tests), a Gecko prototype behind a pref, and a differential parse check of 460k generated cases.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13300/embedded-content-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 4:38 PM UTC (a7af11b)\">/embedded-content-other.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13300/3941bb4...a7af11b/embedded-content-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 4:38 PM UTC (a7af11b)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13300/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 4:38 PM UTC (a7af11b)\">/index.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13300/3941bb4...a7af11b/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 4:38 PM UTC (a7af11b)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13300/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 4:38 PM UTC (a7af11b)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13300/3941bb4...a7af11b/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 4:38 PM UTC (a7af11b)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13300/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 4:38 PM UTC (a7af11b)\">/parsing.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13300/3941bb4...a7af11b/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 4:38 PM UTC (a7af11b)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13300/syntax.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 4:38 PM UTC (a7af11b)\">/syntax.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13300/3941bb4...a7af11b/syntax.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 4:38 PM UTC (a7af11b)\">diff</a> )",
